Both proof stages now close: the first proves the loop theorem directly from the supplied `MPY` semantics; the second reuses that proved theorem as a lemma to prove the public `next_smallest` call from the initial configuration. I’ve encoded those exact stages in `prove.sh` and am doing one clean end-to-end replay, including randomized CPython differential tests and the LLVM `krun` assertions.
